Use a hash map to store each number’s index as you scan the array. For each element `x`, check whether `target - x` has already been seen; if so, return those two indices immediately.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution
{
    public int[] TwoSum(int[] nums, int target)
    {
        var seen = new Dictionary<int, int>();

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.Length; i++)
        {
            int need = target - nums[i];
            if (seen.TryGetValue(need, out int j))
                return new int[] { j, i };

            if (!seen.ContainsKey(nums[i]))
                seen[nums[i]] = i;
        }

        return Array.Empty<int>();
    }
}
```

**Time:** O(n)  
**Space:** O(n)

