Use a hash map from number to index. For each value `x`, check whether `target - x` was seen before; if yes, return those two indices. This is `O(n)` time and `O(n)` space.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    public int[] TwoSum(int[] nums, int target) {
        var seen = new Dictionary<int, int>();

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.Length; i++) {
            long needLong = (long)target - nums[i];
            if (needLong >= int.MinValue && needLong <= int.MaxValue &&
                seen.TryGetValue((int)needLong, out int j)) {
                return new[] { j, i };
            }
            if (!seen.ContainsKey(nums[i])) seen[nums[i]] = i;
        }

        return Array.Empty<int>();
    }
}
```

**Complexity:** `O(n)` time, `O(n)` space.

